4"},{"fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp2pppp/2p5/3p4/3PP3/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQKBNR","san":"d5","fr":"d7","to":"d5"},{"fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp2pppp/2p5/3p4/3PP3/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR","san":"Nc3","fr":"b1","to":"c3"},{"fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp2pppp/2p5/8/3Pp3/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR","san":"dxe4","fr":"d5","to":"e4"},{"fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp2pppp/2p5/8/3PN3/8/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR","san":"Nxe4","fr":"c3","to":"e4"},{"fen":"rnbqkb1r/pp2pppp/2p2n2/8/3PN3/8/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR","san":"Nf6","fr":"g8","to":"f6"},{"fen":"rnbqkb1r/pp2pppp/2p2n2/6N1/3P4/8/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR","san":"Ng5","fr":"e4","to":"g5"},{"fen":"rnbqkb1r/pp2ppp1/2p2n1p/6N1/3P4/8/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR","san":"h6","fr":"h7","to":"h6"},{"fen":"rnbqkb1r/pp2ppp1/2p2n1p/8/3P4/5N2/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR","san":"N5f3","fr":"g5","to":"f3"}],"notes":{"0":{"label":"Start","tag":"","text":"Same opening. We join the game after 4...Nf6.","marks":[]},"9":{"label":"5.Ng5!?","tag":"The alien move","text":"The knight attacks f7.","marks":["f7"]},"10":{"label":"5...h6","tag":"Good defence","text":"Black kicks the knight.","marks":["g5"]},"11":{"label":"6.N5f3","tag":"Do not sacrifice","text":"Do not play 6.Nxf7?. Black takes with the king and you are in trouble (about −2). Retreat calmly.","marks":[]}}}],"chapters":[{"title":"The set-up","kind":"info","tag":"Normal opening","text":"This is the Caro-Kann. Black just chased your knight with <b>4...Nf6</b>. Most players retreat. You will not.","fen":"rnbqkb1r/pp2pppp/2p2n2/8/3PN3/8/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR w KQkq - 1 5","last":{"from":"g8","to":"f6"},"sanline":"1.e4 c6 2.d4 d5 3.Nc3 dxe4 4.Nxe4 Nf6"},{"title":"The alien move: 5.Ng5","kind":"idea","tag":"The idea","text":"The knight jumps again, straight at the f7 pawn. It looks odd, hence the name. The point: Black must now find an accurate answer, and many natural moves lose fast.","fen":"rnbqkb1r/pp2pppp/2p2n2/6N1/3P4/8/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR b KQkq - 2 5","last":{"from":"e4","to":"g5"},"sanline":"1.e4 c6 2.d4 d5 3.Nc3 dxe4 4.Nxe4 Nf6 5.Ng5"},{"title":"Key position: 5...Bf5 6.Bc4","kind":"idea","tag":"Key position","text":"Black develops the bishop, you bring yours. Now both bishop and knight aim at <b>f7</b>. Black has only two safe moves here: <b>6...e6</b> and <b>6...Bg6</b>. Anything else walks into trouble.","fen":"rn1qkb1r/pp2pppp/2p2n2/5bN1/2BP4/8/PPP2PPP/R1BQK1NR b KQkq - 4 6","last":{"from":"f1","to":"c4"},"sanline":"1.e4 c6 2.d4 d5 3.Nc3 dxe4 4.Nxe4 Nf6 5.Ng5 Bf5 6.Bc4"},{"title":"Trap: 6...Nbd7?? 7.Bxf7#","kind":"trap","tag":"Checkmate","text":"The natural developing move is a blunder. The bishop takes on f7, the knight on g5 protects it, and the king has nowhere to go. <b>Checkmate in 7 moves.</b>","fen":"r2qkb1r/pp1npBpp/2p2n2/5bN1/3P4/8/PPP2PPP/R1BQK1NR b KQkq - 0 7","last":{"from":"c4","to":"f7"},"sanline":"1.e4 c6 2.d4 d5 3.Nc3 dxe4 4.Nxe4 Nf6 5.Ng5 Bf5 6.Bc4 Nbd7 7.Bxf7"},{"title":"Black's best: 6...e6","kind":"safe","tag":"Good defence","text":"If Black finds this, calm down and just develop (for example 7.Ne2). The computer prefers Black by about a quarter of a pawn. You still have the better practical chances.","fen":"rn1qkb1r/pp3ppp/2p1pn2/5bN1/2BP4/8/PPP2PPP/R1BQK1NR w KQkq - 0 7","last":{"from":"e7","to":"e6"},"sanline":"1.e4 c6 2.d4 d5 3.Nc3 dxe4 4.Nxe4 Nf6 5.Ng5 Bf5 6.Bc4 e6"},{"title":"Trap: 5...Be6? 6.Nxe6","kind":"trap","tag":"Wins material","text":"Black blocks the f-file with the bishop and your knight simply takes it. Stockfish says about +3 for you.","fen":"rn1qkb1r/pp2pppp/2p1Nn2/8/3P4/8/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR b KQkq - 0 6","last":{"from":"g5","to":"e6"},"sanline":"1.e4 c6 2.d4 d5 3.Nc3 dxe4 4.Nxe4 Nf6 5.Ng5 Be6 6.Nxe6"},{"title":"Trap: 5...Nh5? 6.Bc4","kind":"trap","tag":"Wins big","text":"The knight run to h5 leaves f7 too weak. After 6.Bc4 Stockfish says about +5 for you.","fen":"rnbqkb1r/pp2pppp/2p5/6Nn/2BP4/8/PPP2PPP/R1BQK1NR b KQkq - 4 6","last":{"from":"f1","to":"c4"},"sanline":"1.e4 c6 2.d4 d5 3.Nc3 dxe4 4.Nxe4 Nf6 5.Ng5 Nh5 6.Bc4"},{"title":"Careful: 5...h6 6.N5f3","kind":"warn","tag":"Do not sacrifice","text":"Do not play 6.Nx